  "leaderboardPassHint": "pass with ≈{n} verses",
  "@leaderboardPassHint": {
    "description": "The you-card's advice half, appended after ` · ` and rendered on the LIGHT metric only. `eva/redesign.html:944`; the ÷15 constant is the rail's light economy (`:755`, \"15 per verse read + 10 per correct answer\").\n\nUnder `streaks` it is not rendered at all: a streak gap is not a number of verses.\n\n**The ARABIC arm says نحو and not the prototype's `≈`.** The prototype writes `≈` in both arms (`:944`), and U+2248 is in **no** bundled family that can draw Arabic — Amiri, the Arabic UI family, does not carry it — so the Arabic arm substitutes the word for \"about\". `test/support/font_coverage_test.dart` pins the measurement: U+2248 is absent from Amiri and present in the other four.",
    "placeholders": {
      "n": {
        "type": "String",
        "example": "4"
      }
    }
  },
  "leaderboardNoReset": "no reset · the sky remembers",
  "@leaderboardNoReset": {
    "description": "The reset line for `all_time`: the sky keeps every score, so there is no boundary to count down to. `eva/redesign.html:945` `noReset`, rendered at `:1081`.\n\nPrinted verbatim, including the `·` (U+00B7), which `test/support/font_coverage_test.dart` pins as present in all five bundled families."
  },
  "leaderboardResetsIn": "resets in ≈{days}{dayUnit} {hours}{hourUnit}",
  "@leaderboardResetsIn": {
    "description": "The approximate reset line for a bounded window. `eva/redesign.html:946` `resets`/`dU`/`hU`, composed at `:1082` against a locally derived boundary rather than a server instant.\n\n`{days}`, `{hours}` and the two units are Strings so `digits()` can convert the numerals while the units stay the locale's own words; the `≈` states that the boundary is local (ADR-0022 `:66-81`, `redis/leaderboard.service.ts:20-36`).",
    "placeholders": {
